From: MahanHD <mahanheidari2003@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm: never evict a VRAM carveout object

Without an IOMMU for the display every buffer is a VRAM carveout object,
and these have no shmem file behind them. Under memory pressure, or a
drop_caches, the shrinker still evicted WILLNEED ones: msm_gem_evict()
put_pages() hands the range back to the carveout, and the next use gets
a new range, cleared, with nothing swapped back in. A shader or state
buffer of Xorg's turned into zeros, and every job using it hung the GPU
from then on, every recovery included, until Xorg was restarted: on
this phone, every redraw of the panel clock.

Reproduced on demand: echo 2000 > /sys/kernel/debug/dri/0/shrink, and
Xorg hangs once a minute from then on; restarting Xorg stops it.

Make carveout objects (those with a vram_node, the test get_pages()
already uses) unevictable, and keep the WILLNEED ones on the
pinned LRU, so the shrinker no longer counts them as reclaimable.
DONTNEED ones stay purgeable.

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c	2026-10-12 23:11:55.888486832 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.c	2026-10-15 09:53:45.850769975 +0400
@@ -102,7 +102,15 @@
 	if (msm_obj->pin_count) {
 		drm_gem_lru_move_tail_locked(&priv->lru.pinned, obj);
 	} else if (msm_obj->madv == MSM_MADV_WILLNEED) {
-		drm_gem_lru_move_tail_locked(&priv->lru.willneed, obj);
+		/*
+		 * A carveout object cannot be evicted, so keep it off the list
+		 * the shrinker counts as reclaimable. It can still be purged
+		 * once it is DONTNEED.
+		 */
+		if (!msm_obj->vram_node)
+			drm_gem_lru_move_tail_locked(&priv->lru.willneed, obj);
+		else
+			drm_gem_lru_move_tail_locked(&priv->lru.pinned, obj);
 	} else {
 		GEM_WARN_ON(msm_obj->madv != MSM_MADV_DONTNEED);
 
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.h	2026-10-12 23:11:20.613469356 +0400
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/msm_gem.h	2026-10-15 09:53:45.852233628 +0400
@@ -269,9 +269,13 @@
 	return (msm_obj->vmap_count == 0) && msm_obj->vaddr;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A VRAM carveout object has no shmem file to swap its pages out to:
+ * evicting it hands its range back to the carveout and loses the contents.
+ */
 static inline bool is_unevictable(struct msm_gem_object *msm_obj)
 {
-	return is_unpurgeable(msm_obj) || msm_obj->vaddr;
+	return is_unpurgeable(msm_obj) || msm_obj->vaddr || msm_obj->vram_node;
 }
 
 void msm_gem_purge(struct drm_gem_object *obj);
